I'm playing a serious knight for the first time, and finding Excalibur
and all that holy water to be a great boon.  And it seems I can't get
near an altar but some deity's throwing another artifact at me.

The down side is, all these friendly monsters.  When I played a
barbarian or valkyrie, I hardly noticed the effect except as a minor
part of the game.  But with a knight, *all* the dwarves and tengus are
friendly.  I had to risk the wrath of my god to kill a dwarf for its
pickaxe, and haven't worked up the courage to do the same to a tengu.
After all, I would eat it afterwards, which is surely the path to
damnation.

Two questions:

1) What are all the monsters that are friendly to the different
character types?

2) How can I safely make a friendly monster dead, so that I can eat it
or loot its corpse?  So far with tengus I've tried:

- Scroll/wand of create monster.  Got one unfriendly tengu this way, but
it didn't leave a corpse.  (Neither did the first 15 leprechauns I
killed -- do knights have bad luck this way?)

- Line it up in front of a monster attack.  This could be dragon breath
or giant boulder heave.  I did in a dwarf this way, but he had no
pickaxe.  If I did it for a friendly tengu, would it be safe to eat the
corpse?

- Dig lots of pits and hope it falls in.  This game I'm experimenting
with pits, to see if I can trap things or kill them from a distance.  A
tengu fell in, but wasn't killed and then teleported away.

I guess I could also polymorph something else, but I'm guarding my
polymorph charges carefully.

What else am I missing?  (Besides teleport control that is :-)

John (who's never seen a balrog, even when winning the game)
